"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1195, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:27\", \"token_count\": 363, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-42\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:30] Charlie**: Starting on stream-based chunked reads for large PDFs. Loading the whole document into memory before redacting is what's causing the pressure on bigger files.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:32] Bob**: Makes sense. What's the plan for entities that span a chunk boundary — like an address that gets split across two reads?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:58] Charlie**: Adding a small overlap window between chunks so anything near a boundary gets caught on both sides instead of falling through the gap.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:59] Alice**: Does this help or hurt the multi-threading work?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 12:04] Charlie**: Should help — lower memory per worker means we're not as constrained on how many workers we can run at once.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 12:22] Bob**: Good. Let me know when it's ready for a real large-file test.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 42 slack thread larg file chunk channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 14 2026 08 14 11 30 charli start on stream base chunk read for larg pdfs load the whole document into memori befor redact is what s caus the pressur on bigger file 2026 08 14 11 32 bob make sens what s the plan for entiti that span a chunk boundari like an address that get split across two read 2026 08 14 11 58 charli ad a small overlap window between chunk so anyth near a boundari get caught on both side instead of fall through the gap 2026 08 14 11 59 alic doe this help or hurt the multi thread work 2026 08 14 12 04 charli should help lower memori per worker mean we re not a constrain on how mani worker we can run at onc 2026 08 14 12 22 bob good let me know when it s readi for a real larg file test\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8dbc5b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"id\": \"f9df4a58ad5dbafe\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3394409324219298, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1284467720313283, \"vector_similarity\": 0.83176064, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8dbc5b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 942, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:39\", \"token_count\": 280, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Implemented Approach: Stream Chunking\\n\\nTo keep multi-GB PDFs from being loaded whole into memory, the redaction pipeline now streams large documents in fixed-size page chunks rather than holding the entire document in RAM. This implementation was merged to mainline on 2026-08-16.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Reopen: 2GB+ Leak\\n\\nPost-merge testing on files at and above 2GB surfaced a memory leak: buffers allocated for each chunk were not being released once the chunk finished processing, so peak memory climbed roughly linearly with file size instead of staying bounded by the chunk size. This defeated the point of chunking for the largest files, and the task was reopened as Active (Reopened).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## In-Progress Fix: Per-Chunk Buffer Release\\n\\nCharlie is refactoring the stream-chunk handler to explicitly release each chunk's buffer once processing completes, rather than relying on it falling out of scope. Early local testing on a 2.3GB sample shows flat memory usage across chunks instead of the previous climb, but the fix has not yet been validated against the full large-file test corpus.\\n\\n*Status*: Chunking mechanism is in place and merged; buffer-release refactor to close the 2GB+ leak is still Active and not yet verified end-to-end.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 implement approach stream chunk to keep multi gb pdfs from be load whole into memori the redact pipelin now stream larg document in fix size page chunk rather than hold the entir document in ram this implement wa merg to mainlin on 2026 08 16 sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 reopen 2gb leak post merg test on file at and abov 2gb surfac a memori leak buffer alloc for each chunk were not be releas onc the chunk finish process so peak memori climb rough linear with file size instead of stay bound by the chunk size this defeat the point of chunk for the largest file and the task wa reopen a activ reopen sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 in progress fix per chunk buffer releas charli is refactor the stream chunk handler to explicit releas each chunk s buffer onc process complet rather than reli on it fall out of scope earli local test on a2 3gb sampl show flat memori usag across chunk instead of the previous climb but the fix ha not yet been valid against the full larg file test corpus status chunk mechan is in place and merg buffer releas refactor to close the 2gb leak is still activ and not yet verifi end to end\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9ec20a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"id\": \"dd6eaf806050ad34\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3372607306436095, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13227058520515644, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81557107, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9ec20a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1386, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:46\", \"token_count\": 439, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-43\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:30] Bob**: Reopening large-file chunking. On long-running batches with files over 2GB, memory is still leaking even though the chunked-read path is supposedly done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:31] Charlie**: That's odd, chunking should mean each buffer gets dropped once we move past it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:41] Bob**: It's not the page buffers themselves — something else is holding a reference and keeping them from being freed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:08] Diana**: I can reproduce it in QA too. Memory climbs steadily and the process eventually gets killed on the larger inputs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:20] Charlie**: I'll dig into what's still holding those references. Reopening this until we find it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 43 slack thread larg file chunk reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 18 2026 08 18 10 30 bob reopen larg file chunk on long run batch with file over 2gb memori is still leak even though the chunk read path is suppos done 2026 08 18 10 31 charli that s odd chunk should mean each buffer get drop onc we move past it 2026 08 18 10 41 bob it s not the page buffer themselv someth els is hold a refer and keep them from be freed 2026 08 18 11 08 diana i can reproduc it in qa too memori climb steadili and the process eventu get kill on the larger input 2026 08 18 11 20 charli i ll dig into what s still hold those refer reopen this until we find it\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e91bada88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"e5e49e8fd5982668\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3371745104219298, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1284467720313283, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8242059, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e91bada88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 825, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:48\", \"token_count\": 252, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## The Failure Mode\\n\\nWhen processing massive multi-GB PDF documents (e.g., a 4,000-page merged archive), the loader attempts to load the entire document tree into RAM. For files exceeding 2GB, this consistently results in an `OOMKilled` exception in our standard 4GB Docker containers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## Chunking Implementation\\n\\nWe implemented and merged a \\\"Stream-and-Split\\\" pre-processing layer today. \\n\\n1. The CLI reads the source PDF in 100-page blocks.\\n\\n2. Each block is saved as a temporary sub-document (`doc_part_1.pdf`, `doc_part_2.pdf`).\\n\\n3. The worker pool processes these sub-documents independently.\\n\\n4. A post-processing step merges the redacted sub-documents back into a single final PDF.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## Ordering and Memory Trade-off\\n\\nThis approach solves the RAM issue but introduces a significant disk I/O and ordering overhead. Re-merging the PDFs requires careful tracking of the chunk sequence. Furthermore, if a regex pattern was supposed to match across a page boundary (e.g., a sentence split across pages 100 and 101), the chunking will break the match. We are trading context-awareness for memory stability.\\n\\n*Pending*: We need to run a stress test with a 10,000-page document to verify if the final re-merge step (which also uses RAM) re-introduces the OOM crash.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 the failur mode when process massiv multi gb pdf document e g a4 000 page merg archiv the loader attempt to load the entir document tree into ram for file exceed 2gb this consist result in an oomkil except in our standard 4gb docker contain sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 chunk implement we implement and merg a stream and split pre process layer today 1 the cli read the sourc pdf in 100 page block 2 each block is save a a temporari sub document doc _ part _ 1 pdf doc _ part _ 2 pdf 3 the worker pool process these sub document independ 4 a post process step merg the redact sub document back into a singl final pdf sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 order and memori trade off this approach solv the ram issu but introduc a signific disk i o and order overhead re merg the pdfs requir care track of the chunk sequenc furthermor if a regex pattern wa suppos to match across a page boundari e g a sentenc split across page 100 and 101 the chunk will break the match we are trade context awar for memori stabil pend we need to run a stress test with a 10 000 page document to verifi if the final re merg step which also us ram re introduc the oom crash\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9af1e808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"id\": \"a0395252cfde12bb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32734846970832804, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12741007101189725, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7938714, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9af1e808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1406, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:41\", \"token_count\": 447, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-49\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Memory Leak Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-21\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 09:00] Charlie**: Switching to `tracemalloc` for the leak hunt since the usual profiler is a no-go on the offline lab box. Kicking off a fresh capture now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:05] Charlie**: Already got something. The `tracemalloc` output shows we're holding onto the full page-tree in `RedactionEngine` even after the document object is closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:50] Bob**: That lines up with the hotspot list from earlier this week. I'll start on a patch tonight.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:45] Bob**: Patch is in. Added explicit cleanup so the context manager actually releases the page-tree reference instead of just closing the file handle.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:47] Diana**: Just finished a 6-hour soak test with the new build. Memory usage is flat as a pancake after the initial load. :pancake:\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:41] Alice**: Huge relief. Is this on top of the buffer-release fix from the large-file chunking rework, or a separate code path?\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:43] Bob**: Same family of fix — builds on the chunking buffer-release work. PR #84 is merged.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:44] Evan**: On it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:46] Evan**: Rolling this out to the dev clusters. @Charlie thanks for the tracemalloc deep dive.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 49 slack thread memori leak tracemalloc patch channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 21 last activ 2026 08 23 2026 08 21 09 00 charli switch to tracemalloc for the leak hunt sinc the usual profil is a no go on the offlin lab box kick off a fresh captur now 2026 08 21 11 05 charli alreadi got someth the tracemalloc output show we re hold onto the full page tree in redactionengin even after the document object is close 2026 08 21 11 50 bob that line up with the hotspot list from earlier this week i ll start on a patch tonight 2026 08 23 09 45 bob patch is in ad explicit cleanup so the context manag actual releas the page tree refer instead of just close the file handl 2026 08 23 09 47 diana just finish a 6 hour soak test with the new build memori usag is flat a a pancak after the initi load pancak 2026 08 23 10 41 alic huge relief is this on top of the buffer releas fix from the larg file chunk rework or a separ code path 2026 08 23 10 43 bob same famili of fix build on the chunk buffer releas work pr 84 is merg 2026 08 23 10 44 evan on it 2026 08 23 10 46 evan roll this out to the dev cluster charli thank for the tracemalloc deep dive\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"id\": \"824fb66730068003\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30498601055136687, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11872574364480985, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7395933, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e281228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1379, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:34\", \"token_count\": 428, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-60\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch Workers\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:21] Bob**: The async processing is looking good. I've integrated the progress callbacks so the GUI can show a real-time percentage.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:30] Diana**: I'm seeing some race conditions when two different users try to process the same file simultaneously. The lock isn't being released correctly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:00] Bob**: Ah, I see it. I'm using the filename as the key in the lock manager, but not accounting for the user ID.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:02] Charlie**: Why not use the file hash instead? That way even if they have different filenames but it's the same content, we don't process it twice.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:12] Bob**: Good idea. I'll swap out the keys for the SHA-256 hash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:17] Charlie**: Perfect.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:35] Alice**: @Bob how does this affect the multi-threading work Charlie did?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 16:56] Bob**: They should play well together. The scheduler distributes the *files* to different workers, and each worker uses Charlie's multi-threaded engine to process the *internal* pages.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 60 slack thread async batch worker channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 21 bob the async process is look good i ve integr the progress callback so the gui can show a real time percentag 2026 08 22 14 30 diana i m see some race condit when two differ user tri to process the same file simultan the lock isn t be releas correct 2026 08 22 15 00 bob ah i see it i m use the filenam a the key in the lock manag but not account for the user id 2026 08 22 15 02 charli whi not use the file hash instead that way even if they have differ filenam but it s the same content we don t process it twice 2026 08 22 15 12 bob good idea i ll swap out the key for the sha 256 hash 2026 08 22 15 17 charli perfect 2026 08 22 15 35 alic bob how doe this affect the multi thread work charli did 2026 08 22 16 56 bob they should play well togeth the schedul distribut the file to differ worker and each worker us charli s multi thread engin to process the intern page\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e903a1ae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"id\": \"238bec23f23e7682\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.301603750680804, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10900471525829145, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7510015, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e903a1ae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-22-async-batch-workers.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1171, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:05\", \"token_count\": 352, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nProfile and patch memory-leak hotspots in the PDF loader following signals from the large-file chunking rework. Standard profiler tooling was unavailable in the offline lab, so the team switched to stdlib tracemalloc; the resulting leaks were patched, depending on the large-file chunking path.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Leak hotspots in the PDF loader are identified using an offline-compatible profiling tool.\\n\\n- Identified leaks are patched, verified against the large-file chunking dependency.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nProfile and patch memory-leak hotspots in the PDF loader following signals from the large-file chunking rework. Standard profiler tooling was unavailable in the offline lab, so the team switched to stdlib tracemalloc; the resulting leaks were patched, depending on the large-file chunking path.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-43\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-43\\n\\n**Title**: Find and patch PDF loader memory leaks offline\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-15**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because memory-leak profiling is needed after the large-file chunking work.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-23**: Bob - Tracemalloc Patch (Completed)\\n\\n - *Patched PDF loader leaks found via tracemalloc, depending on the large-file chunking path.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 descript profil and patch memori leak hotspot in the pdf loader follow signal from the larg file chunk rework standard profil tool wa unavail in the offlin lab so the team switch to stdlib tracemalloc the result leak were patch depend on the larg file chunk path clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 accept criterion leak hotspot in the pdf loader are identifi use an offlin compat profil tool identifi leak are patch verifi against the larg file chunk depend clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 descript profil and patch memori leak hotspot in the pdf loader follow signal from the larg file chunk rework standard profil tool wa unavail in the offlin lab so the team switch to stdlib tracemalloc the result leak were patch depend on the larg file chunk path clickup task ciph 43 sourc id src cu ciph 43 task id ciph 43 titl find and patch pdf loader memori leak offlin status complet assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 15 activ histori 2026 08 15 alic task creat open open the task becaus memori leak profil is need after the larg file chunk work 2026 08 23 bob tracemalloc patch complet patch pdf loader leak found via tracemalloc depend on the larg file chunk path\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e982c6b48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"id\": \"6885e4b3a9768baf\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2962946000319208, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10310750004560121, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7470645, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e982c6b48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-43-Memory-Leak-Profiling.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1050, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:18\", \"token_count\": 547, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"CIPH-41 large-file chunking September 22 2026 status Charlie engineering action stress test buffer release\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
