positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.5111959628220438, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.4399421111743484, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67745495, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-42\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:30] Charlie**: Starting on stream-based chunked reads for large PDFs. Loading the whole document into memory before redacting is what's causing the pressure on bigger files.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:32] Bob**: Makes sense. What's the plan for entities that span a chunk boundary — like an address that gets split across two reads?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:58] Charlie**: Adding a small overlap window between chunks so anything near a boundary gets caught on both sides instead of falling through the gap.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 11:59] Alice**: Does this help or hurt the multi-threading work?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 12:04] Charlie**: Should help — lower memory per worker means we're not as constrained on how many workers we can run at once.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 12:22] Bob**: Good. Let me know when it's ready for a real large-file test.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 42 slack thread larg file chunk channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 14 2026 08 14 11 30 charli start on stream base chunk read for larg pdfs load the whole document into memori befor redact is what s caus the pressur on bigger file 2026 08 14 11 32 bob make sens what s the plan for entiti that span a chunk boundari like an address that get split across two read 2026 08 14 11 58 charli ad a small overlap window between chunk so anyth near a boundari get caught on both side instead of fall through the gap 2026 08 14 11 59 alic doe this help or hurt the multi thread work 2026 08 14 12 04 charli should help lower memori per worker mean we re not a constrain on how mani worker we can run at onc 2026 08 14 12 22 bob good let me know when it s readi for a real larg file test\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8dbc5b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"id\": \"f9df4a58ad5dbafe\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4739785545996831, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3154245065709758, \"vector_similarity\": 0.843938, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8dbc5b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-large-file-chunking.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 942, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:39\", \"token_count\": 280, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-44\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Merge\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-16\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:19] Charlie**: Merged the stream-chunking implementation into mainline. Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:21] Alice**: Great, this was overdue. Nice work.\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 09:57] Bob**: Anything left over from the memory concerns during testing, or is it fully clean?\\n\\n**[2026-08-16 10:00] Charlie**: As far as testing showed, clean. We'll see if anything shows up on longer runs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:01] Charlie**: Following up on the leak Bob found on the larger files — root cause was the chunk buffers not being explicitly released once a worker moved past them. Refactoring the buffer-release path now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:15] Bob**: Does the fix release eagerly after each chunk, or wait until the whole file finishes?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:18] Charlie**: Eagerly, right after each chunk is processed — that's the whole point, don't let it accumulate. Still working through it, not ready to call it done again yet.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 09:51] Diana**: Let me know when there's a build to re-run the stress case against.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 44 slack thread larg file chunk merg channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 16 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 08 16 09 19 charli merg the stream chunk implement into mainlin call this done 2026 08 16 09 21 alic great this wa overdu nice work 2026 08 16 09 57 bob anyth left over from the memori concern dure test or is it fulli clean 2026 08 16 1000 charli a far a test show clean we ll see if anyth show up on longer run 2026 08 20 09 01 charli follow up on the leak bob found on the larger file root caus wa the chunk buffer not be explicit releas onc a worker move past them refactor the buffer releas path now 2026 08 20 09 15 bob doe the fix releas eager after each chunk or wait until the whole file finish 2026 08 20 09 18 charli eager right after each chunk is process that s the whole point don t let it accumul still work through it not readi to call it done again yet 2026 08 20 09 51 diana let me know when there s a build to re run the stress case against\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8eb3f568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"id\": \"eff9d8093fd3e4c5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.467790589599683, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3154245065709758, \"vector_similarity\": 0.82331145, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8eb3f568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-16-large-file-chunking-merge.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1195, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:27\", \"token_count\": 363, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.43584392854891685, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.32995658364130986, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6829144, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:36\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"188f8e49d969781d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.43405092064660267, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.31289194378086094, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7167552, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:51\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Authenticated node-replication handshake completes reliably between nodes.\\n\\n- Handshake succeeds under high-latency network conditions, not only nominal latency.\\n\\n- Blocking timeout issue is resolved before multi-site rollout can proceed.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-04**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because multi-site local deployments need distributed zero-trust node synchronization.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-22**: Diana - Handshake Timeout Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after validation showed handshake timeouts on high-latency networks; resolution depends on the encryption work but remains unresolved.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 accept criterion authent node replic handshak complet reliabl between node handshak succeed under high latenc network condit not onli nomin latenc block timeout issu is resolv befor multi site rollout can proceed clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 activ histori 2026 08 04 alic task creat open open the task becaus multi site local deploy need distribut zero trust node synchron 2026 09 22 diana handshak timeout block block block after valid show handshak timeout on high latenc network resolut depend on the encrypt work but remain unresolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e993c5728a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"d487d4d51c3b088f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4299156885489169, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.32995658364130986, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6631536, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e993c5728a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1197, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:05\", \"token_count\": 534, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## The Failure Mode\\n\\nWhen processing massive multi-GB PDF documents (e.g., a 4,000-page merged archive), the loader attempts to load the entire document tree into RAM. For files exceeding 2GB, this consistently results in an `OOMKilled` exception in our standard 4GB Docker containers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## Chunking Implementation\\n\\nWe implemented and merged a \\\"Stream-and-Split\\\" pre-processing layer today. \\n\\n1. The CLI reads the source PDF in 100-page blocks.\\n\\n2. Each block is saved as a temporary sub-document (`doc_part_1.pdf`, `doc_part_2.pdf`).\\n\\n3. The worker pool processes these sub-documents independently.\\n\\n4. A post-processing step merges the redacted sub-documents back into a single final PDF.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-25\\n\\n# Design Note: Large File Chunking Strategy\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2025\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n## Ordering and Memory Trade-off\\n\\nThis approach solves the RAM issue but introduces a significant disk I/O and ordering overhead. Re-merging the PDFs requires careful tracking of the chunk sequence. Furthermore, if a regex pattern was supposed to match across a page boundary (e.g., a sentence split across pages 100 and 101), the chunking will break the match. We are trading context-awareness for memory stability.\\n\\n*Pending*: We need to run a stress test with a 10,000-page document to verify if the final re-merge step (which also uses RAM) re-introduces the OOM crash.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 the failur mode when process massiv multi gb pdf document e g a4 000 page merg archiv the loader attempt to load the entir document tree into ram for file exceed 2gb this consist result in an oomkil except in our standard 4gb docker contain sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 chunk implement we implement and merg a stream and split pre process layer today 1 the cli read the sourc pdf in 100 page block 2 each block is save a a temporari sub document doc _ part _ 1 pdf doc _ part _ 2 pdf 3 the worker pool process these sub document independ 4 a post process step merg the redact sub document back into a singl final pdf sourc id src gdoc 25 design note larg file chunk strategi owner charli document key doc 2025 last updat 2026 08 14 order and memori trade off this approach solv the ram issu but introduc a signific disk i o and order overhead re merg the pdfs requir care track of the chunk sequenc furthermor if a regex pattern wa suppos to match across a page boundari e g a sentenc split across page 100 and 101 the chunk will break the match we are trade context awar for memori stabil pend we need to run a stress test with a 10 000 page document to verifi if the final re merg step which also us ram re introduc the oom crash\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9af1e808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"id\": \"a0395252cfde12bb\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.41718784708426504, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24210082154895007, \"vector_similarity\": 0.82572424, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9af1e808a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-14-Large-File-Chunking-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1406, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:41\", \"token_count\": 447, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Implemented Approach: Stream Chunking\\n\\nTo keep multi-GB PDFs from being loaded whole into memory, the redaction pipeline now streams large documents in fixed-size page chunks rather than holding the entire document in RAM. This implementation was merged to mainline on 2026-08-16.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Reopen: 2GB+ Leak\\n\\nPost-merge testing on files at and above 2GB surfaced a memory leak: buffers allocated for each chunk were not being released once the chunk finished processing, so peak memory climbed roughly linearly with file size instead of staying bounded by the chunk size. This defeated the point of chunking for the largest files, and the task was reopened as Active (Reopened).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-42\\n\\n# Design Review: Large-File Chunking — Post-Merge Reopen\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2042\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## In-Progress Fix: Per-Chunk Buffer Release\\n\\nCharlie is refactoring the stream-chunk handler to explicitly release each chunk's buffer once processing completes, rather than relying on it falling out of scope. Early local testing on a 2.3GB sample shows flat memory usage across chunks instead of the previous climb, but the fix has not yet been validated against the full large-file test corpus.\\n\\n*Status*: Chunking mechanism is in place and merged; buffer-release refactor to close the 2GB+ leak is still Active and not yet verified end-to-end.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 implement approach stream chunk to keep multi gb pdfs from be load whole into memori the redact pipelin now stream larg document in fix size page chunk rather than hold the entir document in ram this implement wa merg to mainlin on 2026 08 16 sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 reopen 2gb leak post merg test on file at and abov 2gb surfac a memori leak buffer alloc for each chunk were not be releas onc the chunk finish process so peak memori climb rough linear with file size instead of stay bound by the chunk size this defeat the point of chunk for the largest file and the task wa reopen a activ reopen sourc id src gdoc 42 design review larg file chunk post merg reopen owner charli document key doc 2042 last updat 2026 08 23 in progress fix per chunk buffer releas charli is refactor the stream chunk handler to explicit releas each chunk s buffer onc process complet rather than reli on it fall out of scope earli local test on a2 3gb sampl show flat memori usag across chunk instead of the previous climb but the fix ha not yet been valid against the full larg file test corpus status chunk mechan is in place and merg buffer releas refactor to close the 2gb leak is still activ and not yet verifi end to end\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9ec20a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"id\": \"dd6eaf806050ad34\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.41538422308426504, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24210082154895007, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81971216, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9ec20a08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-23-Large-File-Chunking-Design-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1386, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:46\", \"token_count\": 439, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-43\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:30] Bob**: Reopening large-file chunking. On long-running batches with files over 2GB, memory is still leaking even though the chunked-read path is supposedly done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:31] Charlie**: That's odd, chunking should mean each buffer gets dropped once we move past it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:41] Bob**: It's not the page buffers themselves — something else is holding a reference and keeping them from being freed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:08] Diana**: I can reproduce it in QA too. Memory climbs steadily and the process eventually gets killed on the larger inputs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:20] Charlie**: I'll dig into what's still holding those references. Reopening this until we find it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 43 slack thread larg file chunk reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 18 2026 08 18 10 30 bob reopen larg file chunk on long run batch with file over 2gb memori is still leak even though the chunk read path is suppos done 2026 08 18 10 31 charli that s odd chunk should mean each buffer get drop onc we move past it 2026 08 18 10 41 bob it s not the page buffer themselv someth els is hold a refer and keep them from be freed 2026 08 18 11 08 diana i can reproduc it in qa too memori climb steadili and the process eventu get kill on the larger input 2026 08 18 11 20 charli i ll dig into what s still hold those refer reopen this until we find it\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e91bada88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"e5e49e8fd5982668\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.41427600508426504, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.24210082154895007, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8160181, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e91bada88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 825, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:48\", \"token_count\": 252, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd stream chunking so large, multi-GB PDF documents can be processed without excessive memory pressure. Chunking was merged, but the task was reopened after files over 2GB were found to still leak memory; buffer-release logic is being refactored to release buffers after each chunk.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Large PDF documents are processed via stream chunking rather than loading whole files into memory.\\n\\n- Memory buffers are released after each chunk, with no leak on files 2GB and larger.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd stream chunking so large, multi-GB PDF documents can be processed without excessive memory pressure. Chunking was merged, but the task was reopened after files over 2GB were found to still leak memory; buffer-release logic is being refactored to release buffers after each chunk.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-41\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-41\\n\\n**Title**: Stream-chunk multi-GB PDF loads without retaining buffers\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-12**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because large-file chunking is needed for multi-GB documents.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-20**: Charlie - Buffer Release Refactor (Active (Reopened))\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 41 sourc id src cu ciph 4